<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">NKVD Order No. 00447</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1937">1937</a>–<a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Order No. 00447</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a> Order No. 00447 of 30 July 1937 was signed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikolai-yezhov">Nikolai Yezhov</a> and approved by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/politburo">Politburo</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-purge">Great Purge</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. It ordered kulaks and other so-called anti-Soviet elements to be divided into two categories, the first to be shot and the second sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulag">Gulag</a> labour camps, and set quotas for each territory, to be met in a speedy and simplified way. Sentences were passed by troikas of the regional NKVD chief, the prosecutor and the Party secretary, and executions were held in secret. The quotas were exceeded many times over: by the end of 1938 the NKVD had executed 386,798 Soviet citizens under the order.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nkvd-order-no-00447.jpg" alt="NKVD Order No. 00447" width="330" height="536" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NKVD of USSR · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NKVD_Order_No._00447.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
